=== Trouble Brewing ===
{{Obsolete|15 January update}}
[[File:Scrapey tree logs detail.png|left|frameless|width=50x50]]
With 40 [[Cooking]] and the completion of [[Cabin Fever]], players can enter [[Trouble Brewing]]. Games of Trouble Brewing can be played consistently on [[World]] 304, or on any world with another player. Within the minigame, there is a variety of activities that can be completed with very low initial stats. Players wishing to train Fletching can bring a Woodcutting axe and take a knife from the [[Workbench (Trouble Brewing, tools)|Workbench]] to cut [[Scrapey tree|Scrapey trees]]. These give [[Scrapey tree logs]] that can be fletched into [[Scrapey bark]] for 50 Fletching experience each. These can additionally be deposited upstairs in the [[Hopper (Trouble Brewing)|Hopper]] for 100 Cooking experience each.

With a [[Rune axe]] and 41+ Woodcutting, experience rates of over 30k Fletching experience, 16k Woodcutting experience, and 60k Cooking experience per hour can be achieved with no upfront costs or supplies.

Certain strategies may also increase potential experience rates. Dropping scrapey bark instead of depositing it can enable higher experience rates in Fletching and Woodcutting, albeit sacrificing the potential Cooking experience. Cutting from the west side pairs of scrapey trees can minimize downtime if done with no competition, which is consistently possible on a world with only one player on each team.

===Darts===
[[File:Toxic blowpipe detail.png|left|frameless|width=50x50]]
High-level to mid-level players who have the [[toxic blowpipe]] will need to make [[dart]]s to use it. [[Adamant dart]]s are easy to obtain and provide decent experience. [[Amethyst dart]]s are the highest level darts that can be gathered and provide significant bonuses over adamant darts.

As this section is highly dependent on Smithing, players may also want to consider either fletching or stringing bows, or making more arrows and crossbow bolts, as they will need plenty of ammunition for ranging. Bows can be sold for a small amount at [[Lowe's Archery Emporium]].

===Vale Totems===
[[File:Beautiful tree stump.png|left|50px]]
With the completion of [[Vale totems]] miniquest, players can construct and decorate totem sites around [[Auburnvale]]. This [[minigame]] is an active Fletching method with experience rates dependent on the wood used for constructing the totem and for fletching the decorations used on the totem. Rewards for this activity also include [[Vale Research Points]], bird nests, tree roots, [[dirty arrowtips]], [[Bale of flax|bales of flax]], and [[Ent branch|ent branches]]. 

At maximum efficiency, Vale Totems offers the highest Fletching experience rates per hour that a player can achieve without monetary investment. The most efficient experience rates are achieved with: a stockpile of logs in the bank, carrying a log basket, running the route to construct and decorate 8 totem sites around [[Auburnvale]], all while Fletching and stringing bows between totem sites. At that rate,players can expect to earn approximately 8000 [[Vale offerings]] per hour, which is equivalent to 80 [[Vale Research Points]]. 

Less effective methods are available for those who wish to train [[Woodcutting]] at the same time, or who do not have a stockpile of logs available, where a player sticks to a single totem while cutting nearby trees until the totem site decays. 

